      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if it results from a sudden, accidental, and covered event\u2014such as a severe windstorm, hail, falling tree limbs, or heavy snow/ice accumulation. It generally does not cover leaks caused by normal wear and tear, aging materials, or a lack of routine home maintenance.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Covered vs. Not Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Covered Causes:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "High winds blowing off shingles or flashing during a storm\n."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Hail bruising or puncturing roofing materials."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Heavy snow, ice dams, or sudden structural collapse."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Falling trees, limbs, or flying debris."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Resulting interior water damage to ceilings, walls, or personal belongings (if caused by a covered storm)."
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Excluded Causes:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Gradual leaks or rotting wood from old age\n."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Neglect or failure to fix known minor roof flaws."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Poor original installation or faulty building materials."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Damage from earthquakes or floods (which require separate specialized policies)\n."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Steps to Take"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you experience a dispute or need consumer guidance regarding a denied claim, you can review details or contact the\nUtah Insurance Department\nfor assistance.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like more specific guidance, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What caused the leak\n(a recent storm, aging shingles, etc.)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What type of damage inside or outside the home you are seeing?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you understand how to approach your specific situation."
      }
    ],
